1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Coffee Chat Copilot turns a job opportunity into a conversation, with your own voice and review before every message.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:16,000
This is a real LinkedIn people search. In the installed extension, import visible results from the tab beside the panel.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The remaining screens use fictional contacts to demonstrate the workflow. This browser preview does not perform a real LinkedIn import.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Review each contact and their source context. An email guess is only a guess, and needs your independent confirmation.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Write your outreach once. The template keeps your wording while placeholders adapt the message to a job and contact.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Every draft enters your approval queue. Edit, regenerate, skip, or approve it. Approval alone never sends an email.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:02,000
These are the Google setup controls. Authorization is not recorded here. Live Gmail and Calendar access requires your own consent in Chrome.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Once a time is agreed, choose it in the meeting form. This is a demo; no real calendar invitation is sent.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Build a question bank by adding, editing, or skipping suggestions. Only approved bank questions are selected for your prep brief.

10
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The prep view brings context and approved questions together, so you can spend the conversation listening instead of searching.

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
After the chat, save a few notes. Review a thank-you draft and decide whether to include the optional referral paragraph.

12
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The activity view keeps next steps together. This walkthrough sent no real emails or invitations. You stay in control.
